From b3e202e779ebb770da26d21d1992c727e92e1f1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 21:13:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v1.6.1: Auto Scan refinements - dedup-by-block,
 terminate-on-leave, progress, report, QoL

Live pre-validation showed the candidate selection was wrong (an arbitrary
spread could scan redundant same-block channels and skip the clean one);
rwifi_scan_candidates now keeps one PSC representative per physical 320 block -
the 6 real positions across both 320-1/320-2 sub-grids.

Auto Scan UX:
- terminate the sweep if the tab is closed / navigated away: the browser poll
  is a heartbeat (the worker aborts + restores the channel when it goes stale)
  plus a sendBeacon(scanstop) on pagehide for an instant stop.
- progress bar (candidates done/total, active pulse) + ETA.
- keep the admin session alive during the scan; the normal idle timeout resumes
  on its own when the scan ends.
- mark the current channel in results; best-vs-current on the Pin confirm;
  pinned toast; friendly "capture running" busy message.
- syslog one-line winner summary; capture noise floor (knoise) per candidate.

Downloadable report: a self-contained landscape HTML document (Print / Save PDF
via a hidden print iframe, or Download) with the ranked table (incl. noise
floor) and an SVG spectrum plot placing each 320 block by frequency, colored by
occupancy with direct labels + legend.

i18n: RWIF_50-57 across all 25 language dicts, lockstep.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
